TY  - JOUR
T1  - Investigating the Relationship between Governance and Economic Growth in Developing Countries
AN  - 2267397631
AB  - The different economic performance of countries can be derived from the type of governance they adopt. Good governance is evaluated through six indices that have been calculated by world bank for different countries; voice and accountability, political stability and lack of violence, government effectiveness, regulatory quality, rule of law and corruption control. In addition, the performance of each country depends on its long-term economic growth rate. Thus, one of the goals of each economy is to achieve the high economic growth rates. This paper examines the impact of good governance on the economic growth using panel data procedure for the period 19962013. The results suggest a negative relationship between inflation and government expenditure and economic growth and a positive and statistically significant relationship between labor and trade openness and economic growth and also suggest that there is a positive relationship between good governance indices and growth.
