TY  - JOUR
T1  - World Cup bribery allegations crown unhappy year for Qatar.
AN  - 1617179638; 0001212854
AB  - Even before the bribery allegations concerning the Qatar bid to host the 2022 World Cup, this gas-rich emirate has been increasingly under pressure, especially from its neighbours like Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates. This comes from its support for rebel groups in the Arab uprisings as well as criticism of its labour conditions affecting the workers building the football stadia; it risks losing its popularity with contractors to a resurgent Dubai property market, and the new Emir is under pressure to cut its high public spending levels.
