TY  - JOUR
T1  - Corruption-its effects
AN  - 743149679; 201004-30-0285567 (CE)
AB  - In Nigeria they call it dash, in Malaysia it's known as money politics, in Britain as just plain sleaze. Whatever the label, corruption can undermine democracy, distort priorities and worsen poverty. For corruption diverts public expenditure away from key sectors such as health and education to more immediately lucrative ones such as construction and defense. Richer countries could help reduce corruption by doing more to eliminate poverty in developing countries, and by ensuring that their own procedures do not aid the bribers. Yet Britain's Export Credits Guarantee Department, a government body that provides guarantees and insurance for British companies seeking contracts abroad, is criticized in a recent report from UK-based NGO Corner House, "Turning a Blind Eye: Corruption and the UK's Export Credits Guarantee Department," which examines 9 ECGD-backed projects where corruption has been alleged.
