TY  - JOUR
T1  - China's Western Development Program: Its Rationale, Implementation, and Prospects
AN  - 60608081; 200309743
AB  - Examines the development program in the western regions of the People's Republic of China, particularly its focus on economic, regional, ecological, & security concerns. Following an analysis of the program's implementation in terms of economic adjustment, infrastructure, investment, environment, human capital, & general welfare, discussion shifts to the program's future prospects -- its obstacles & advantages. It is opined that the number & nature of obstacles -- in particular, corruption, inefficiency, & ethnic division -- may lessen the economic & political benefits from the program's implementation, especially in regions with large ethnic populations. 6 Tables, 58 References. S. Stanton
