TY  - JOUR
T1  - Transportation Policy in Mexico City: The Politics and Impacts of Privatization
AN  - 61611023; 9814615
AB  - Examines the impacts of transportation privatization in Mexico City via a cost-&-benefit analysis, drawing on interview data from 380 Federal District residents & 30 public officials, government data, & newspaper reports. Privatization has reduced direct government spending in some areas but has exacerbated economic inequities, political corruption, traffic congestion, & injuries & fatalities, as well as air pollution & related illness & mortality. Transport policy has benefited the federal district, affluent residents, & service providers, but the users & poor who live in marginal zones have received fewer benefits. 5 Tables, 44 References. Adapted from the source document.
